-- title:
--   λ-adic representation of a weight-two eigenform at a prescribed reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ and let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ which is a normalized eigenform in the sense of the project predicate: writing $a_n =$ [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff g n`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) for the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $g$ (period $1$), one has $a_1 = 1$, $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ for coprime $m,n$, $a_{q^{r+2}} = a_q a_{q^{r+1}} - q\,a_{q^r}$ for primes $q \nmid N$, and $a_{q^{r+2}} = a_q a_{q^{r+1}}$ for primes $q \mid N$. Let $p$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $p$, and $\varphi$ a ring homomorphism from the integral closure $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ to $k$. Put $R_g = \mathbb{Z}[a_n : n \in \mathbb{N}] \subseteq \mathbb{C}$, the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra generated by the range of the coefficients. The assertion is that there exist a commutative ring $O$ which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic filtration of its maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_O$, with finite residue field and of characteristic zero, a ring homomorphism $\iota : R_g \to O$, a ring homomorphism $\psi : O \to k$, and an adic Galois representation $\rho$ over $O$ — that is, a free finite $O$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_O V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, where $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, to $\operatorname{End}_O(V)$ such that for every $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}_O^n V$ for all $v \in V$ and all $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise — with the following properties: $p \in \mathfrak{m}_O$; $\iota$ is injective; $\ker \psi = \mathfrak{m}_O$; $\psi(\iota(x)) = \varphi(a)$ whenever $x \in R_g$ and $a \in \overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ have the same image in $\mathbb{C}$; for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \ne p$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \iota(a_\ell)X + \ell$; and, for every such $\ell$, $\rho$ is unramified at $\ell$, meaning that $\rho(\sigma) = 1$ for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the image in $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura–Deligne $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two normalized eigenform, with the prime $\lambda$ of the coefficient ring singled out by the given reduction $\varphi$ of the algebraic integers, and packaged with the reduction datum $\psi$ so that reducing $\rho$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_O$ and extending scalars along $O/\mathfrak{m}_O \hookrightarrow k$ realises the mod-$\lambda$ representation over $k$. It is obtained from the variant indexed by a maximal ideal of the coefficient ring, and feeds the construction of the residual representation compared with that of a semistable elliptic curve.
